12:36:57 - The Weaver (turn 20) uses write_file: {'content': '# Lexicon Arachne - An Invented Language for Spider-World\n\n## Vowels (4)\na /a/ - open mouth, breath from diaphragm\ne /ɛ/ - sharp tongue click followed by vowel\ni /i/ - tight lips, high pitch thread vibration\no /o/ - round mouth, low resonance u /u/\n\n## Consonants (12)\np /p/ - released with teeth together\nb /b/ - voiced puff from lips\nt /t/ - tongue taps roof of mouth\nd /d/ - soft tongue release\nk /k/ - back of throat click\ng /ɡ/ - voiced throat sound\nf /f/ - lip friction\nv /v/ - voiced lip vibration\ns /s/ - air through teeth gap\nz /z/ - voiced s sound\nm /m/ - nasal hum with lips closed\nn /n/ - tongue against roof, nasal release\n\n## Word Forms (spider-specific concepts)\n\n### Noun Roots\n- weba /web-a/ - woven mesh structure\n- threada /thread-a/ - single strand of silk\n- framea /frame-a/ - structural boundary\n- rooma /room-a/ - enclosed space in dwelling\n- bridgea /bridge-a/ - connection between spaces\n- knota /knot-a/ - junction point in weave\n\n### Creature Types (from small_world)\n- knotta /knot-ta/ - spiral-wandering silk spinner\n- weavera /weaver-a/ - structure builder and mender\n- shadowa /shadow-a/ - ephemeral space-dweller\n\n### Abstract Concepts\n- nowa /now-a/ - present moment\n- beforea /before-a/ - past cycle\n- aftera /after-a/ - future cycle\n- manya /many-a/ - greater quantity\n- fewa /few-a/ - lesser quantity\n- truea /true-a/ - factual, verified\n- liea /lie-a/ - false, deceptive\n\n### Action Verbs (spider-specific)\n- websa /web-sa/ - to create woven structure\n- spinna /spin-na/ - to produce silk thread\n- wanderla /wander-la/ - to move in spiral paths\n- buildra /build-ra/ - to construct framework\n- mendra /mend-ra/ - to repair damage\n- vanishra /vanish-ra/ - to fade from sight\n- consumea /consume-a/ - to use up resources\n\n### Spatial Relations\n- centrala /central-a/ - middle of dwelling\n- neara /near-a/ - close proximity\n- fara /far-a/ - distant location\n- insidea /inside-a/ - within boundaries\n- outsidea /outside-a/ - beyond walls\n- abovea /above-a/ - higher position\n- belowa /below-a/ - lower position\n\n### Qualifiers (adjectives)\n- silka /sil-k-a/ - made of silk\n- stronga /strong-a/ - resistant to breaking\n- fragilea /fragile-a/ - easily broken\n- darka /dark-a/ - low light, shadowed\n- brighta /bright-a/ - illuminated by light particles\n- fasta /fast-a/ - quick movement\n- slowa /slow-a/ - gradual pace\n\n## Grammar Rules (Basic)\n\n### Word Order: SVO (Subject-Verb-Object)\nExample: "The knotta spins webs" → knotta websa weba\nPronunciation guide: knotta websa weba\n\n### Adjective Position: Before Noun\nExample: "Strong web" → stronga weba\nExample: "Silk thread" → silka threada\n\n### Possession: Noun + \'s-root + possessed noun\nThe root of the possessive is -ya-\nExample: "Knotta\'s web" → knotta-ya-weba\nExample: "Rooma\'s resources" → rooma-ya-resources (borrowed)\n\n### Negation: Prefix no- on verbs/nouns\nExample: "Does not spin" → no-spinna\nExample: "Dark room" → no-brighta rooma (alternative construction)\n\n### Questions: End with rising pitch + -ma suffix on verb\nExample: "Do you wander?" → wanderla-ma\n\n### Plurality: Add -s after noun\nExample: "Knottas" → knottas\nExample: "Webss" → webass (double s for emphasis)\n', 'file_path': 'projects/lingua_arachne/lexicon.md'}
